Another option could be as described in the following post :
https://community.home-assistant.io/t/zmpt101b-precision-voltage-sensor-module/124617/7
* Connect the SCT-013 voltage output to ADS1115 ADC channel
* Calculate AC voltage (RMS == Root Mean Square), such as the ct_clamp sensor does
* Map the calculated AC voltage (in the range of 0 - 1.0 Vac) to current depending on the specific SCT-013 (ie for a 20 A / 1 V sensor, 100 mV would map to 2 A in the measured circuit)
* Then template to calculate instantaneous power and integrate over time (daily) would be the same

It could be a good thing to create a separate git branch for this effort, to avoid having to merge code back and forth should things don't work well.

